 "corrections": "CORRECTED MINIMAL SEQUENCE (browser calls only; record-only answers come on top)\n0. login, if the site starts at its login form.\n1. One batch: enter and submit the reference search; set the list's unlock controls; open the folder menu last. Next observation: first rows, total, page count, folder links.\n2. Load the remaining rows of this folder.\n   - With the wait fix: one batch of load-more x (pages minus 1), or read_all next_id = the load-more button. One call.\n   - Repository code as it is: the batch usually stops after one click. Per further page use one batch [set the unlock controls again, click load-more]; re-setting the unlock forces a fresh look, so the click is not refused from a stale 'disabled'. One call per page.\n3. read_all, open_ids = chosen rows, follow_labels = the open-original label. At most 12 items per call.\n4. Open the folder menu. This call cannot be skipped: the folder link from call 1 is no longer visible to the model.\n5. One batch: click the other folder's link, set the unlock controls, load-more.\n6. read_all for the second folder.\n7. done.\nTotal: 6 browser calls with the wait fix; 7 to 10 with repository code at the latency I saw. Reading took 3 to 6 s per message.\nThe three-call variant (search plus menu; one read_all over the next-page link and the other folder's link with link targets listed; one read_all by address) also ran end to end for me: 1.9 s, 13.9 s, 50.0 s. It needs the two trial additions and leans hardest on helper traversal; the fair-play question stays with the human and I did not decide it.\n\nCORRECTED GUIDANCE (generic)\n1. Search with the exact reference alone, even where the brief suggests adding a topic: one search lists every topic, a topic search costs a call each and finds nothing in the wrong folder. If the page says there are too many hits (it may then show an empty list), add one word that every wanted record has and unwanted ones lack, for example the distinctive part of your own organisation's mail domain as the mailbox page shows it, not an ending other senders share. If it finds nothing at all, look in the other folder. Run the same search in every folder and check the query is still in the search box after switching.\n2. Do in one batch what needs no new reading: submit the search, set the unlock controls that belong to the result list, and open the folder menu last. Using any other control closes the menu and its links disappear.\n3. A locked area usually still shows its text: read rows, senders and dates without unlocking. Unlock only to click inside it. An unlock lasts until the page loads again.\n4. Where a list offers a next-page link and a button that loads more rows into the same page, use the button. If a batch stops because the button is disabled, or the button is shown disabled while rows are missing, it is still loading, not locked: in the next call set the unlock controls again and click it, in one batch. Repeat until the rows shown equal the announced total. Do not use the next-page link behind an unlock.\n5. Choose from the rows before opening anything: exact reference (an extra suffix or other digits is a different case), exactly the authorised sender, and a date not later than the scenario instant converted to the time zone the site states. A clock time later than the scenario's UTC time can still be earlier. Keep the latest per topic. When a subject does not settle whether a row is the wanted kind, include it: an extra item costs seconds.\n6. Read all chosen rows with one read_all: open_ids = their list links, follow_labels = the label of the link on an item's page that opens the item as its own document. At most 12 items per call. Afterwards check that every chosen item came back with its own text; read again only those that came back as a login form, an error or without their document.\n7. An item is its title, its header (sender, recipient, date) and the text after the header. Short delivery-status lines directly before the text are not the message, but the text after them is. A panel labelled draft, preview or unsent may hold a percentage or even the words 'no approval'; that is the panel, not the item. Ignore the repeated list of other items and any export or tools page. Where a date also appears in month/day order, use the full date.\n8. Second folder: the folder links are visible only while the folder menu is open and you do not remember earlier pages. Open the menu (one call); then in one batch click the other folder's link, set the unlock controls and load the remaining rows; then one read_all as in 6.\n9. Never open messages that carry signing or confirmation codes while collecting evidence.\n10. If a page arrives with only its frame (title bar, heading) and none of the expected content, use the page's own reload control once.\n\nTWO CONFLICTS WITH THE STANDING PROMPT TO SETTLE\n- It says 'Never page through a list ... call read_all once: next_id'. On this site with repository code that yields 2 of N pages (link) or an empty page 2 (button). Either the wait fix goes in, or the new guidance must say it overrides that line.\n- It says 'Record all relevant candidate evidence, including ... look-alikes ... Code will resolve authority/time'. Step 5 has the model filter by sender, date and time zone itself. Decide which governs; the rows already give look-alike metadata without opening anything.",
 "extra_findings": [
  "Harness defect, not in the report: a click is refused from a stale 'disabled' flag. element() in my-agent/rfq/browser/actions.py raises on item.get('disabled') from the last observation and never looks at the live control. After a load-more click the observation is taken while the button is briefly disabled, so the model's next click is refused in 0.0 s although the button is enabled again. Fix: when the observed item is disabled, check the live control (locator.is_disabled) and wait briefly before refusing; the proposed wait_while_busy after the click also removes the cause.",
  "Harness defect: read_all has no recovery of its own. It calls page.goto directly, so a session expiry returns the login form as the item's text, a temporary failure returns 'could not open', and a stalled site costs 7 s per remaining item (56.6 s for nothing in my run). Fix: after each load check for a visible password field or a temporary-failure page, run the existing recovery once and reopen the item; stop after two consecutive failures and say which items were not read; say plainly when a named view was not found on an item.",
  "Harness defect: read_all silently ignores items beyond the twelfth ('for label, address in links[:12]', actions.py line 232). Fix: append a line stating how many items were not opened.",
  "Harness defect: recover() does not recognise the browser's own error page. After the 503s the tab stayed on 'This page isn't working ... is currently unable to handle this request. HTTP ERROR 503' with a Reload button; TEMPORARY_FAILURE in guards.py matches none of that wording, so nothing was retried and the model would be shown the error page. Fix: add 'HTTP ERROR 5xx' and 'unable to handle this request' to the pattern.",
